    "body": "[A10] **Acceptance item 2: 10 consecutive hosted runs at `f41e4f2d`.** All are attempts 1 to 10 of rtl-fast run 38162821680 (`pull_request`). Times are job wall-clock from the Actions API. Every job concluded success in every attempt.\n\n| Attempt | firmware-unit | firmware-control-mutants | firmware-srp-mutants | firmware-aecp-mutants |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 1 | 684 s | 682 s | 567 s | 239 s |\n| 2 | 703 s | 841 s | 415 s | 243 s |\n| 3 | 676 s | 823 s | 577 s | 174 s |\n| 4 | 667 s | 831 s | 595 s | 250 s |\n| 5 | 660 s | 840 s | 482 s | 242 s |\n| 6 | 538 s | 815 s | 610 s | 207 s |\n| 7 | 534 s | 838 s | 604 s | 169 s |\n| 8 | 667 s | 826 s | 625 s | 260 s |\n| 9 | 449 s | 648 s | 505 s | 203 s |\n| 10 | 693 s | 830 s | 604 s | 244 s |\n| **Slowest / 2700 s** | **703 s (26.0 %)** | **841 s (31.1 %)** | **625 s (23.1 %)** | **260 s (9.6 %)** |\n\nThe slowest job over the 10 runs is `firmware-control-mutants` at 841 s, 31.1 % of its 45-minute timeout. The bound is 70 % (1,890 s), so item 2 is met. The author's conservative prediction for that job was 879 s.\n",
